PrintBridge slicer image
========================

This image contains OrcaSlicer @ORCA_VERSION@, a 3D printing slicer.

  OrcaSlicer is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
  version 3 (AGPL-3.0). The licence text is in /opt/orca/LICENSE.txt.
  Source code of this exact version:
    https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer/tree/v@ORCA_VERSION@
    https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer/archive/refs/tags/v@ORCA_VERSION@.tar.gz
  The source archive is also attached to every PrintBridge release:
    https://github.com/Beauver/PrintBridge/releases

What this image changes compared to OrcaSlicer's release:

  - /opt/orca is OrcaSlicer's official Linux AppImage
    (OrcaSlicer_Linux_AppImage_Ubuntu2404_V@ORCA_VERSION@.AppImage), unpacked.
    No program files are modified.
  - Files only the graphical interface uses were removed from
    /opt/orca/resources: hms, i18n, images, web, textures, handy_models,
    calib, tooltip, fonts, tools and Icon.icns.
  - /opt/profiles holds OrcaSlicer's system profiles (resources/profiles/*.json
    from the same release tag), unchanged.
  - /opt/orca/resources/profiles/<vendor>/<kind>_full/ holds profiles generated
    from those: each profile with its inherited settings merged in, so the
    command line finds them. They are created by /app/slicer_service.py
    (--write-full-profiles) while building the image.

The HTTP wrapper /app/slicer_service.py is part of PrintBridge, licensed
under the GNU AGPL-3.0-or-later:
  https://github.com/Beauver/PrintBridge

The Debian packages in this image keep their own copyright and licence files
under /usr/share/doc.
